"We wanted seven, but we'll take five"

Brendan Rodgers

We won our 7th league and 5th trophy in a row since Brendan came in at Parkhead in front of the Rangers fans. We sang Halliday's name every time he took a throw-in or did anything in the game. We sang Alfredo Morelos' name when he was subbed on.

**Forrest** scored against Rangers. PC Lustig was born. PC Lustig made a blatant pocketed gesture at Jamie Murphy. **Scott Brown** ruffled Candeias' hair like he was a wee boy. **KT** took the GB's megaphone and led the celebrations.

Rangers banned their staff from speaking to the media. Our whole team to a man played phenomenally well, our fans rubbed it in their faces for 90 minutes and our manager loved it all as much as we did.

These are really special times. Take time to savour these league titles, these absolute hammerings of the reborn Rangers. 30 years ago, we won the league in our centenary season. 20 years ago, we won the league to stop them doing 10. 10 years ago, we won the league on a Thursday night for Tommy Burns. Today – nothing but complete domination and an annihilation of Rangers, their support and their camp followers.

Enjoy your celebrations, bhoys and ghirls, this is the time of our lives.

WHAT MEMBERS OF THE MEDIA SAID

@mstewart_23: Who is actually making the decision at Rangers to not speak to any media? Can't imagine it's Murty or any board members. Perfectly illustrates how the club is desperately lacking real leadership.

@BBCTomEnglish: Celtic ragdolled Rangers today. A vast humiliation. I feel sorry for Graeme Murty. He's getting dog's abuse. The fault lies well above his head.

@McGregorDerek: Rangers gutless off the park too. No manager or player prepared or allowed to come up to face the media.

@mrjakehumphrey: Well done Brendan. Well done Celtic. I imagine Steven Gerrard was watching that Rangers mess, and instead of being daunted, realising how much better he can make them…

